083533 1071 "Find all of the real solutions to the equation $8{z}^{3}-{z}^{2}+40z-5=0.$" 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186083533 1074 "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{z}^{3}-{z}^{2}+40z-5 & = \\\\ (8{z}^{3}-{z}^{2})+(40z-5) & = \\\\ {z}^{2}(8z-1)+5(8z-1) & = \\\\ (8z-1)\\cdot {z}^{2}+(8z-1)\\cdot 5 & = \\\\ (8z-1)({z}^{2}+5) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(8z-1)({z}^{2}+5)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(8z-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8z-1 & =0 \\\\ 8z & =1 \\\\ z & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({z}^{2}+5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince a squared real number cannot be negative, the equation ${z}^{2}+5=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore,  $z=\\frac{1}{8}$ is the only real solution." 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186085789 13194139536023 17592186045417 false] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186085790 13194139536023 17592186045417 false] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186085791 13194139536023 17592186045417 false] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186085792 13194139536023 17592186045417 false] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186085793 13194139536023 17592186045417 false] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557907 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186557945 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558079 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558164 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186085788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186558318 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186085788 1078 #edb/ref 17592186557907 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186087759 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558538 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186087769 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558542 13194139536023 17592