tly, the recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n$$\na_{n+1}= a_n + 5, \\quad a_1=4, \\quad n\\geq 1\\,.\n$$" 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186179637 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558509 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186179637 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558526 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186179638 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558521 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186179638 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558565 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186179849 1050 420.0 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186180786 1064 "Suppose we have the following arithmetic sequence with first term\n\n$$\na_1 = {\\color{red}4}\n$$\n\nand common difference\n\n$$\nd={\\color{blue}{3}}\n$$\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{4}},7,10,13,16,\\ldots\n$$\n\nEach term is ${\\color{blue}{3}}$ more than the previous, starting with ${\\color{red}{4}}$. Therefore, we can express this sequence recursively:\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + {\\color{blue}{3}}, \\quad a_1 = {\\color{red}{4}}, \\quad n\\geq 1\n$$\n\nWe can also express the sequence using function notation:\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = f(n) + {\\color{blue}{3}}, \\quad f(1) = {\\color{red}{4}}, \\quad n\\geq 1\n$$" 13194139536023 17592186045417 false] [17592186180786 1064 "Suppose we have the following arithmetic sequence with first term $a_1 = {\\color{red}4}$ and common difference  $d={\\color{blue}{3}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{4}},7,10,13,16,\\ldots\n$$\n\nEach term is ${\\color{blue}{3}}$ more than the previous, starting with ${\\color{red}{4}}.$ Therefore, we can express this sequence recursively:\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + {\\color{blue}{3}}, \\quad a_1 = {\\color{red}{4}}, \\quad n\\geq 1\n$$\n\nWe can also express the sequence using function notation:\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = f(n) + {\\color{blue}{3}}, \\quad f(1) = {\\color{red}{4}}, \\quad n\\geq 1\n$$" 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186198434 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558485 13194139536023 17592186045417 true] [17592186221420 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558553 13194139536023 175